# m2asc — no commit unless asked

**Never run `git commit` (or stage-for-commit as a prelude to committing) unless the user clearly requests a commit in that message.**

## Counts as permission

- User runs `/m2asc-ship` (after review approval), or
- User explicitly says to commit (e.g. “commit this”, “create a commit”, “commit the docs rename”)

## Does NOT count as permission

- “We’ll do this in separate commits” / “each step gets a commit” (process preference only)
- “Go ahead” / “implement” / “rename” / “do the next step” without the word commit/ship
- Finishing a leaf and setting `🔍` — propose a message; **do not** commit
- Implied convenience (“cleaner history if I commit now”)

If unclear: **do not commit** — leave changes in the working tree and ask.

See also: `m2asc-no-push` (never push, even if asked).
